### Batch Gate System
- **Code gate** in `classify_art_v2.py`: `check_batch_gate()` blocks batches >5 games if gate closed. `close_batch_gate()` auto-closes after every batch. `update_gate_from_regression()` auto-opens if **theme ≥97% AND overall ≥95%** + fixes applied. No bypass flag.
- **Gate file** `art_pipeline/batch_gate.json`: Missing = CLOSED (fail-safe). `gate_open` defaults to false.
- **Cursor rule** `.cursor/rules/art-pipeline-gates.mdc`: Always-applied stop-fix-verify cycle.
- **Thresholds**: ≥85% spot-check auto-open after fixes; 75-84% needs fixes+verification; <75% escalate

### Compliance Hook System (session 9)
- **5 project hooks** in `.cursor/hooks.json` — fire for ALL agents (Atlas, Art, Dev)
- `sessionStart`: Injects live data counts, gate status, drift detection (agent-neutral)
- `preToolUse` (Write|StrReplace|Delete): HARD BLOCK on 6 protected pipeline data files (`failClosed`)
- `beforeShellExecution`: Blocks rm -rf on data dirs, --force-gate, force push. Flags large batches (cost guard)
- `afterFileEdit`: Tracks edited files by category (art_pipeline, dev_code, config_rules)
- `stop`: Forces ONE verification loop after edits — tailored by file category (regression for art, tests for dev)

